WEBVTT

00:55.990 --> 00:58.868
FILING FOR LOVE

01:02.413 --> 01:05.875
EPISODE 12:
BECAUSE I LOVE YOU

01:47.708 --> 01:51.795
36 HOURS BEFORE M&amp;A

01:58.928 --> 02:00.012
Would you like a drink?

02:00.095 --> 02:01.972
I don't think there's anything
left for us to talk about.

02:03.307 --> 02:04.391
No, wait.

02:06.268 --> 02:08.896
"Regret lingers more over the things
we never did than the things we did.

02:09.188 --> 02:12.608
And unrequited love lasts longer
than love that has faced its end."

02:13.651 --> 02:14.735
Do you remember saying that?

02:17.112 --> 02:19.240
"Attempt everything. Never stop.

02:19.573 --> 02:23.035
I will not let you end up regretting
the things you didn't do at Haemu."

02:24.828 --> 02:26.413
It's a quote
from your inaugural address

02:27.331 --> 02:29.416
that impressed me a great deal.

02:33.295 --> 02:34.547
Keep your word.

02:35.422 --> 02:36.924
Don't make me regret anything.

02:46.600 --> 02:48.477
What a waste of good liquor.

02:50.563 --> 02:51.855
I quit drinking.

02:54.066 --> 02:55.442
I'll finish it, then.

03:05.828 --> 03:07.079
You have a good memory.

03:08.581 --> 03:10.207
Even I'd forgotten I'd said that.

03:11.375 --> 03:13.711
I believed you were
a pretty decent leader.

03:15.045 --> 03:16.046
Back then, that is.

03:19.300 --> 03:20.551
That hits hard.

03:23.721 --> 03:25.097
I mean it.

03:25.431 --> 03:26.640
It was around the time

03:27.641 --> 03:29.476
I'd started to look down on Haemu.

03:30.311 --> 03:32.104
My superiors were fools

03:32.187 --> 03:33.897
and my coworkers were frustrating.

03:34.648 --> 03:36.233
The company seemed small.

03:42.281 --> 03:43.282
Yes.

03:43.657 --> 03:45.659
I was an arrogant punk.

03:46.660 --> 03:48.203
I thought my life

03:48.912 --> 03:52.374
was a straight highway
with no obstacles at all.

03:53.250 --> 03:54.960
That is, until I met Ms. Joo.

03:55.461 --> 03:59.465
In-a must've pulled the brakes
on your smooth-sailing life

04:00.215 --> 04:01.717
when she demoted you
to handle PM cases.

04:01.967 --> 04:03.260
Reality hit hard.

04:03.969 --> 04:05.929
I thought,
"Why should I be doing this stuff?"

04:07.264 --> 04:08.932
Not long after that

04:09.308 --> 04:10.851
I started to feel ashamed.

04:12.561 --> 04:16.523
To me, Haemu was just a place
to do well, be acknowledged

04:16.732 --> 04:18.901
and prove myself to others.

04:21.111 --> 04:22.196
To someone else

04:23.155 --> 04:25.199
Haemu was a source of pride.

04:25.783 --> 04:28.160
- Please excuse me.
- It was a part of an enjoyable day

04:38.170 --> 04:41.298
and something they had to protect
at all costs.

04:41.757 --> 04:43.759
- Let's go!
- I realized that Haemu

04:43.842 --> 04:47.012
- Cheers!
- is where people come to work.

04:50.724 --> 04:52.893
I'd like you to think
of those very people.

04:53.977 --> 04:55.270
You wouldn't want

04:57.606 --> 04:59.358
to leave with regrets, would you?

05:28.554 --> 05:29.555
JEON JAE-YEOL

05:32.349 --> 05:33.434
Hello?

05:36.603 --> 05:37.604
What?

05:40.107 --> 05:41.817
Please excuse my intrusion.

05:52.327 --> 05:54.538
- Coffee?
- No, thanks.

05:54.621 --> 05:55.831
I'll get him out of here right away.

05:57.666 --> 05:59.793
Mr. Noh, get up this instant.

06:00.335 --> 06:02.921
Hey, Ms. Joo, when did you get here?

06:03.005 --> 06:04.631
How much did you drink?

06:05.466 --> 06:08.469
- Are you the only one hungover?
- I guess so.

06:08.802 --> 06:11.305
I don't think I drank that much,
but I must've dozed off.

06:14.475 --> 06:15.893
What's this?

06:18.270 --> 06:19.730
Did you cover me up with this?

06:20.564 --> 06:22.483
How sweet of you.

06:23.734 --> 06:25.527
That's enough nonsense.

06:26.403 --> 06:27.446
Let's get to the point.

06:29.031 --> 06:30.032
What now?

06:30.532 --> 06:32.284
What do you need me to do?

06:34.036 --> 06:36.330
Did you change your mind?

06:40.584 --> 06:42.753
Mr. Noh tells a pretty good story.

06:51.553 --> 06:52.888
24 HOURS BEFORE M&amp;A

06:52.971 --> 06:55.808
The main subsidiaries
will be sold off tomorrow.

06:55.891 --> 06:58.852
So you want to hold a board meeting
and dismiss Sung-yeol before then?

06:58.936 --> 07:00.187
Yes, that's right.

07:00.270 --> 07:03.398
Out of the directors,
Director Woo is most against the M&amp;A.

07:03.899 --> 07:07.319
Meet Director Woo
and persuade him to call the meeting.

07:07.402 --> 07:09.822
I'm not saying
I'll return to management.

07:10.113 --> 07:11.865
I want to break from tradition

07:11.949 --> 07:13.867
and hire a management specialist.

07:14.660 --> 07:18.539
Do you think you can
achieve that on your own?

07:18.789 --> 07:20.290
Some employees are on my side.

07:20.374 --> 07:22.125
There will be a change
from the roots up.

07:23.919 --> 07:25.838
I won't be leading from the front.

07:26.505 --> 07:28.006
I'll be supporting from behind.

07:28.382 --> 07:30.384
When Director Woo calls the board

07:30.509 --> 07:33.846
we must persuade a majority
of the other directors to attend.

07:33.929 --> 07:35.889
This is the only way to stop the M&amp;A.

07:35.973 --> 07:37.558
We can't manage on our own.

07:38.016 --> 07:39.685
I'll ask Team Three for their help.

07:42.771 --> 07:44.606
That's Director Yoon over there.

07:44.690 --> 07:46.316
Yes. I see him.

07:48.569 --> 07:50.821
AIRPORT TERMINAL

08:01.957 --> 08:04.835
- Oh, hello, sir.
- What are you doing?

08:04.918 --> 08:06.169
You can't leave.

08:15.012 --> 08:16.263
- Please help.
- Oh, gosh.

08:19.057 --> 08:20.058
JEON SUNG-YEOL

08:20.142 --> 08:21.268
An emergency board meeting?

08:24.771 --> 08:27.524
So Jae-yeol has started to move.

08:28.734 --> 08:30.527
It's fine as long as the majority
doesn't attend.

08:31.528 --> 08:34.781
Director Park and Director Jeong
won't be interested anyway.

08:35.824 --> 08:38.035
- Call Director Ha.
- Yes, sir.

08:38.911 --> 08:39.995
Oh, one more thing.

08:40.537 --> 08:43.999
Be sure the deal
to sell HM Trans is on track.

08:44.249 --> 08:45.792
Sure, I understand.

08:49.129 --> 08:51.715
3 HOURS BEFORE M&amp;A

08:56.303 --> 08:57.429
How did it go?

08:57.638 --> 08:59.389
Director Ha didn't come
to the meeting place.

08:59.473 --> 09:00.766
He won't take our calls, either.

09:01.600 --> 09:04.311
I think he sided with Jeon Sung-yeol.

09:09.983 --> 09:11.568
They'll be signing the deal soon.

09:19.242 --> 09:20.661
President Jeon.

09:21.828 --> 09:23.914
He's still a registered board member.

09:24.873 --> 09:26.166
Forget it.

09:26.833 --> 09:28.627
I have no reason to do that.

09:30.295 --> 09:31.588
The game is over already.

09:32.756 --> 09:36.093
You lost to him completely
at the shareholders' meeting.

09:37.094 --> 09:38.637
I don't want to side with a loser.

09:40.514 --> 09:41.765
Father.

09:42.265 --> 09:44.017
What did I fight for all this time?

09:45.352 --> 09:48.814
The reason I spent my entire life
trying to win and earn recognition

09:49.314 --> 09:51.608
in the fight you set up for me

09:53.026 --> 09:55.988
is that I understood
the purpose of that fight.

09:56.613 --> 09:59.032
"The strongest shall survive
to lead Haemu."

10:00.158 --> 10:01.576
I believed that, too.

10:02.953 --> 10:05.080
But look at Haemu now.

10:05.163 --> 10:07.624
Look at the company
you tried to protect.

10:09.835 --> 10:11.169
Is this how you want it to be?

10:14.047 --> 10:15.674
You had once told me

10:16.091 --> 10:20.178
that protecting something
means discarding everything else.

10:24.099 --> 10:26.268
I came here to protect Haemu.

10:26.601 --> 10:29.771
I gave up on an ordinary life,
my pathetic ego

10:32.816 --> 10:36.028
and my hatred and resentment for you.

10:38.613 --> 10:40.949
So, will you please put aside
your disappointment in me

10:42.325 --> 10:43.994
for a short while?

10:46.413 --> 10:47.706
For Haemu's sake.

10:49.374 --> 10:52.127
MARCH 11, 2026
SIGNED BY JEON SUNG-YEOL

11:15.525 --> 11:17.319
What do you think you're doing?

11:17.402 --> 11:19.696
The deal you just signed is invalid.

11:20.447 --> 11:22.783
The board dismissed VP Jeon Sung-yeol

11:23.742 --> 11:26.078
and he has no right to sign the deal.

11:26.369 --> 11:28.497
What stupid prank is this?

11:28.914 --> 11:31.166
We already signed
and exchanged the papers.

11:32.292 --> 11:35.170
The board passed the resolution
to remove you

11:35.253 --> 11:37.214
at 2:25 p.m. on March 11, 2026.

11:38.173 --> 11:40.217
According to Article 17
of Haemu's company charter

11:40.634 --> 11:42.427
you lose all authority

11:43.637 --> 11:45.597
the moment you are dismissed.

11:49.893 --> 11:51.269
That's impossible.

11:52.187 --> 11:53.313
VOTING RESULTS
TO DISMISS VP JEON SUNG-YEOL

11:53.396 --> 11:56.066
What is this? How come...

11:56.983 --> 12:00.153
- Ms. Park, where is Director Ha?
- He's at his residence.

12:01.113 --> 12:02.322
Then who else signed this?

12:05.534 --> 12:06.827
Father?

12:06.910 --> 12:07.994
DISMISSAL OF AN EXECUTIVE

12:08.078 --> 12:09.412
PRESIDENT JEON MOO-TAE

12:09.496 --> 12:11.456
Why would Father sign...

12:11.540 --> 12:13.458
What on earth is going on?

12:13.542 --> 12:16.753
We informed your company
as soon as the resolution passed.

12:16.837 --> 12:18.672
I'm sure you don't want to face
the legal risk

12:18.755 --> 12:20.465
of signing a deal
with an unauthorized proxy.

12:21.299 --> 12:24.886
The emergency board meeting
adhered to all laws and charters.

12:25.720 --> 12:27.639
If you still want to challenge
its validity

12:28.849 --> 12:30.308
we'll meet you in court.

12:47.576 --> 12:48.994
When did you set this up?

12:50.370 --> 12:52.497
You acted like
you didn't care or want anything.

12:53.415 --> 12:55.125
Were you hiding your talons
all this time?

12:57.419 --> 12:59.004
I'm not here to steal what's yours.

13:00.755 --> 13:02.799
I'm here
so I can leave without regret.

13:35.373 --> 13:36.917
How typical of him
to leave behind a mess.

13:37.250 --> 13:41.338
I think he destroyed the files
that could pose a problem later on.

13:45.175 --> 13:46.718
I kept backup copies.

13:50.305 --> 13:51.681
You're still very meticulous.

13:52.933 --> 13:54.392
That's how you took me down.

13:57.896 --> 13:59.356
Why did you change your mind?

14:01.149 --> 14:02.317
I realized

14:04.611 --> 14:07.239
I wasn't as bad a person
as I thought.

14:40.230 --> 14:42.857
Man, it was like
a scene from a movie.

14:42.941 --> 14:44.901
It was more film-like than a film.

14:45.277 --> 14:47.445
Guess how many times Hae-young and I
drove around the golf club.

14:47.529 --> 14:49.656
You all had a partner, at least.

14:49.739 --> 14:52.784
I went on my own
to Director Min's home.

14:53.118 --> 14:56.288
You know he has the worst temper
out of all the directors, don't you?

14:56.371 --> 14:58.748
- Come on.
- His temper isn't the worst.

14:58.832 --> 15:01.459
We had to deal with Director Yoon
who put up a fight.

15:01.543 --> 15:04.254
- Right?
- Right, and we subdued him.

15:05.380 --> 15:07.674
We almost had to board a plane.

15:14.639 --> 15:16.266
Great work today.

15:17.767 --> 15:19.602
I owe it to them for their help.

15:20.061 --> 15:22.981
We couldn't have done it without you.

15:24.357 --> 15:25.692
Good job.

15:28.653 --> 15:30.363
Is Jae-yeol joining us for dinner?

15:31.781 --> 15:33.783
Why don't you give him a call?

15:33.867 --> 15:35.744
You two met up just fine without me.

15:37.203 --> 15:38.830
It is a shame.

15:39.414 --> 15:41.958
If we hadn't met
as your ex and current boyfriend

15:42.042 --> 15:43.710
we could've been really close.

15:46.087 --> 15:47.297
I mean it.

15:48.006 --> 15:50.133
I see why you dated him.

15:50.425 --> 15:51.509
He's pretty cool.

15:52.969 --> 15:55.180
You're cool, too.
You don't seem jealous.

15:56.264 --> 15:57.557
Why would I be jealous?

15:59.267 --> 16:01.353
I'm the one you're with now.

16:03.104 --> 16:05.648
Who cares? They all know.

16:05.732 --> 16:07.567
Mr. Noh... Hey, what's going on?

16:07.817 --> 16:09.361
Are you two holding hands?

16:09.444 --> 16:11.654
Are you holding hands
in the open now?

16:11.738 --> 16:14.324
Why don't you two treat us all?

16:17.285 --> 16:19.871
Yes, we're holding hands,
and we'll treat you all!

16:20.205 --> 16:22.207
- Yes!
- Let's eat!

16:23.666 --> 16:25.877
- How about beef?
- Sounds good.

16:27.796 --> 16:29.339
Beef is expensive.

16:30.006 --> 16:31.966
- No beef?
- Come on...

16:42.560 --> 16:46.523
1 YEAR LATER

16:46.606 --> 16:48.566
HEAD OF SALES DIVISION, LIM HYEOK-JUN

17:00.412 --> 17:01.955
The target's on the move.

17:02.372 --> 17:03.665
Oh, over.

17:16.177 --> 17:17.929
Target's on the move. Stand by, Tail.

17:49.043 --> 17:51.254
Target found. I'm tailing him.

17:56.801 --> 17:58.052
Oh, shoot.

18:03.057 --> 18:04.309
Let's go.

18:44.682 --> 18:47.227
We were right on the money.

18:48.353 --> 18:49.479
You're up.

18:51.648 --> 18:52.982
Be careful.

18:58.571 --> 18:59.739
We're moving in.

19:00.823 --> 19:01.824
Go on.

19:05.245 --> 19:06.871
Are we really going in?

19:09.207 --> 19:10.208
Hey.

19:11.668 --> 19:12.877
Step aside.

19:14.629 --> 19:15.880
Director Lim!

19:19.717 --> 19:20.969
Stop what you're doing.

19:21.052 --> 19:22.512
We're from the Audit Team.

19:23.888 --> 19:26.099
What are you doing here?

19:26.516 --> 19:28.101
You said you were out on business.

19:28.184 --> 19:29.852
What are you selling here?

19:31.646 --> 19:35.149
I wanted to spruce up
before meeting my sales contacts.

19:35.608 --> 19:36.651
I'm trying to look clean.

19:37.193 --> 19:40.822
Coming to a bathhouse
to spruce up during work hours

19:41.197 --> 19:43.074
is a dereliction of duty.

19:43.449 --> 19:45.827
Even more so if you do it every day.

19:54.460 --> 19:56.254
Rookie, get a hold of yourself.

19:56.588 --> 19:59.340
I told you to move in.
Why did you hesitate?

19:59.632 --> 20:01.843
What if we missed our opportunity?

20:02.468 --> 20:04.178
Nothing that bad would've happened.

20:05.138 --> 20:07.807
- Pardon?
- That's the truth.

20:07.890 --> 20:10.268
And I don't see
why we must do this anyway.

20:10.602 --> 20:13.980
I studied in the US and did well
on Haemu's entrance exam.

20:14.731 --> 20:15.940
I don't get

20:16.482 --> 20:19.110
why I should do this stuff.

20:24.532 --> 20:25.658
This "stuff"?

20:27.827 --> 20:28.870
Who do you think you are?

20:28.953 --> 20:30.830
Do you have superpowers? Can you fly?

20:30.913 --> 20:32.915
Can you teleport or do a palm blast?

20:37.003 --> 20:39.255
No rookie has the right
to decide what to do or not.

20:40.965 --> 20:42.383
Don't look down on what we do.

20:43.259 --> 20:47.555
Everything the Audit Team does
is equally important.

20:49.682 --> 20:52.143
Don't you think that sounds familiar?

20:52.226 --> 20:53.645
- Yes.
- Right?

20:53.728 --> 20:56.147
It's all good.
You caught him red-handed.

20:56.230 --> 20:57.815
You did well.

20:58.149 --> 21:01.319
- Don't neglect your health.
- Thank you.

21:02.362 --> 21:04.197
Here you go, Mr. Noh.

21:07.325 --> 21:08.409
And our rookie.

21:09.118 --> 21:10.244
Thank you.

21:12.914 --> 21:13.915
You smiled?

21:18.586 --> 21:19.754
Did you just smile?

21:23.716 --> 21:26.886
I like that. You should smile.
Smiling brings fortune.

21:28.554 --> 21:29.722
Thank you.

21:31.808 --> 21:33.184
Here's some for Team Two.

21:33.518 --> 21:35.353
Stay healthy.

21:36.229 --> 21:37.897
Am I the only one who finds this odd?

21:37.980 --> 21:40.108
There's no middle ground.
She's so extreme.

21:40.191 --> 21:42.610
It feels like they're starting
to swap personalities.

21:43.152 --> 21:45.446
They say you grow alike
with the one you love.

21:59.001 --> 22:01.879
How is life abroad?
Is your mother well?

22:02.296 --> 22:03.840
I like the peace and quiet.

22:04.173 --> 22:05.550
My mother settled in right away.

22:06.634 --> 22:08.970
I flew in to handle something else.

22:09.554 --> 22:11.472
I didn't think I'd run into you here.

22:13.391 --> 22:16.144
You wouldn't take my calls,
so I had to get creative.

22:23.735 --> 22:26.320
We're developing
a new medication to target

22:26.404 --> 22:27.947
treatment-resistant mental illnesses.

22:28.364 --> 22:31.033
The roadmap takes into account
possible medical clusters.

22:31.451 --> 22:33.161
We've already signed
R&amp;D partnership MOUs

22:33.244 --> 22:35.872
with several
major university hospitals in Korea.

22:36.539 --> 22:38.708
What we need now are investments.

22:39.542 --> 22:42.587
But this is a large-scale project
beyond the foundation's capacity.

22:44.130 --> 22:46.340
We desperately need
your connections and wisdom.

22:47.300 --> 22:48.926
JEI MEDICAL FOUNDATION
CNS RESEARCH CENTER

22:53.639 --> 22:55.224
Jei Medical Foundation

22:56.309 --> 22:58.519
went through a rough patch
because of me.

22:59.604 --> 23:03.232
Won't my involvement
harm their image?

23:03.441 --> 23:08.404
Everyone knows how devoted you were
to helping your mother.

23:08.780 --> 23:11.574
What motive could be
stronger than sincerity?

23:24.295 --> 23:26.255
It looks delicious.

23:29.926 --> 23:31.636
Mr. Noh Ki-jun.

23:31.928 --> 23:34.472
Why are you so hard on the rookie?

23:35.181 --> 23:36.849
He was close to bursting into tears.

23:36.933 --> 23:40.603
Come on. Since when did you become
such a caring boss?

23:40.686 --> 23:42.188
Think of how you treated me.

23:43.105 --> 23:45.817
And that is how you become
a mean-spirited superior.

23:52.740 --> 23:54.367
It's so good.

23:55.326 --> 23:56.869
Doesn't it look easy to make?

23:56.953 --> 23:57.995
I should give it a try.

24:01.332 --> 24:05.378
You seem oddly upbeat today.

24:11.425 --> 24:12.510
Well...

24:13.803 --> 24:16.305
I have something to tell you.
Hang on.

24:20.059 --> 24:21.060
So...

24:21.811 --> 24:23.229
I bought a place.

24:23.479 --> 24:24.814
- A house?
- Yes.

24:24.897 --> 24:27.149
A short-term rental? No.
A long-term rental? No.

24:27.233 --> 24:28.609
It's completely my own.

24:29.068 --> 24:31.988
The building's a bit old,
but it's perfect for one person

24:32.071 --> 24:33.531
and it's close to where you live.

24:33.614 --> 24:35.032
Isn't that just great?

24:35.116 --> 24:36.617
Yes, but...

24:36.909 --> 24:38.244
did you want to move?

24:38.327 --> 24:41.914
My landlord suddenly asked me to move
so he could move in.

24:41.998 --> 24:43.624
I had to rush to find a new place

24:43.708 --> 24:45.751
and I came across
an apartment for sale.

24:45.835 --> 24:48.045
I decided to take the plunge
and buy a place outright.

24:59.724 --> 25:00.933
The reason

25:01.017 --> 25:04.020
I didn't tell you is that
I didn't want to cause you trouble.

25:04.103 --> 25:05.855
- You're already busy with work.
- You know

25:05.938 --> 25:09.108
we see each other at work every day
and eat dinner afterward.

25:09.191 --> 25:11.068
We even go on dates on weekends.

25:11.152 --> 25:14.655
We tell each other everything,
yet you had no time to tell me that?

25:15.656 --> 25:18.284
What I'm saying is,
I didn't tell you.

25:19.619 --> 25:21.537
I don't like it
when you worry about me.

25:23.372 --> 25:25.207
Sure. I know what you're like.

25:26.167 --> 25:29.462
I'll try to understand that
you have issues you don't tell me.

25:29.921 --> 25:31.088
That's what you're like.

25:33.090 --> 25:35.801
I'm sorry. Don't be angry, okay?

25:35.885 --> 25:37.887
So you went and bought an apartment?

25:38.554 --> 25:40.097
Perfect for one person?

25:41.307 --> 25:42.516
That means

25:43.267 --> 25:45.186
you have no intentions
of living with me.

25:46.979 --> 25:47.980
Well...

25:50.524 --> 25:52.693
We practically live together
right now.

25:52.777 --> 25:56.405
- You come over or I come to yours.
- Exactly. We do that now.

25:56.489 --> 25:58.282
Don't you want to move in?

25:59.784 --> 26:01.577
Are you saying
we should live together?

26:05.289 --> 26:06.374
Wait...

26:06.958 --> 26:07.959
A marriage?

26:10.378 --> 26:12.546
- Are you insane?
- Excuse me? "Insane"?

26:12.630 --> 26:14.090
Marriage?

26:14.173 --> 26:16.842
- Why would I marry?
- Why wouldn't you?

26:17.969 --> 26:18.970
It's just...

26:19.345 --> 26:21.305
I won't. I don't do marriages.

26:22.098 --> 26:24.141
Not even with me?

26:25.559 --> 26:26.686
That's...

26:28.771 --> 26:30.231
I never thought about it.

26:33.359 --> 26:34.694
Then start thinking about it.

26:35.236 --> 26:36.779
What? But...

26:38.030 --> 26:41.075
That's too one-sided on your part.
It's a huge decision.

26:43.327 --> 26:45.037
You called me a variable.

26:45.705 --> 26:47.915
An unexpected variable
that entered your life.

26:50.418 --> 26:51.836
I don't want to be that anymore.

26:53.254 --> 26:54.755
I want us to talk and discuss

26:54.839 --> 26:57.675
our plans ten or 20 years later
until the day we die.

26:59.051 --> 27:00.720
I want to plan everything with you.

27:01.554 --> 27:05.266
I want to be a constant in your life.

27:06.267 --> 27:07.435
Ki-jun.

27:08.310 --> 27:11.272
- You have your own life.
- It can be our life.

27:12.148 --> 27:13.566
A life we share together.

27:38.466 --> 27:39.550
CONCLUSION AND EXPECTED BENEFITS

27:39.633 --> 27:42.470
Separating the Audit Team isn't about
changing the organizational chart.

27:42.970 --> 27:45.389
We want to be independent
of the managerial executives

27:45.473 --> 27:48.100
to avoid being influenced
by internal politics.

27:48.184 --> 27:51.020
It's a structural shift
that allows us to stand alone.

27:51.604 --> 27:53.439
There will be
many initial difficulties

27:53.522 --> 27:56.776
but it can become a reality
if the company and we are determined.

27:56.859 --> 28:00.029
I believe it's a system
that must be implemented.

28:01.113 --> 28:03.324
That concludes my explanation
of the roadmap.

28:06.994 --> 28:08.454
You have no questions, do you?

28:08.537 --> 28:11.373
You must be very busy.
You can return upstairs...

28:15.336 --> 28:16.420
Mr. Noh?

28:18.339 --> 28:20.549
What happens when we're separated
from other departments

28:20.758 --> 28:23.969
preventing us from accessing data
due to security risks?

28:24.595 --> 28:26.972
Won't we have to beg others
for information?

28:28.933 --> 28:31.310
The board approved this move.

28:31.393 --> 28:34.355
We're guaranteed
unlimited access to all data

28:34.438 --> 28:37.733
and Head of IT will be
held accountable if they refuse.

28:37.817 --> 28:39.068
What about the budget?

28:39.151 --> 28:41.612
We'll lose our customary speed
if we can't sign anything

28:41.695 --> 28:42.822
without the board's approval.

28:42.905 --> 28:44.824
We only need approval
for our annual budget.

28:44.907 --> 28:47.409
The Head of Audit
will allocate the necessary funds.

28:47.493 --> 28:51.163
They're all ideals
that look good on paper.

28:51.247 --> 28:53.207
What if we try to break free
from management

28:53.290 --> 28:55.793
only to have to tiptoe around
all the other departments?

28:59.338 --> 29:00.589
It doesn't look like

29:01.090 --> 29:03.217
you tiptoe around anyone at work.

29:05.219 --> 29:06.846
Am I wrong?

29:19.483 --> 29:21.152
That was intense.

29:21.235 --> 29:22.695
I almost wet myself.

29:23.112 --> 29:24.196
Me, too.

29:24.280 --> 29:27.783
Mr. Noh challenged Ms. Joo
a bit too much in public.

29:27.867 --> 29:29.451
I see why he would, though.

29:29.535 --> 29:30.995
Ms. Joo was too harsh on him.

29:31.412 --> 29:33.497
Everyone pretends to have forgotten,
but I remember.

29:33.581 --> 29:38.335
Ms. Joo went to the reporters
and told them that she used Ki-jun

29:38.419 --> 29:40.296
then came back
without so much as an apology.

29:40.379 --> 29:42.047
Mr. Noh must hate it.

29:42.756 --> 29:45.009
Could there still be

29:45.134 --> 29:47.887
something between them?

29:48.304 --> 29:51.849
- Like what?
- Forget about her using him.

29:51.932 --> 29:53.475
They had something going on.

29:54.268 --> 29:57.104
- Yes.
- And lashing out like that here...

29:57.188 --> 29:59.815
- It's not like that!
- Have you heard, Mr. Sung?

30:00.566 --> 30:02.818
Mr. Oh from Planning
and Ms. Seon from Finance

30:02.902 --> 30:04.904
are getting married.
Isn't that crazy?

30:07.740 --> 30:09.533
Yes, I heard about that.

30:10.075 --> 30:12.286
- He must have an idea.
- Yes, right.

30:12.369 --> 30:14.079
- You can...
- Team One.

30:14.163 --> 30:17.249
The expense... Where is
this quarter's expense report?

30:19.001 --> 30:20.169
You want that now?

30:23.672 --> 30:25.174
Something's fishy.

30:28.928 --> 30:30.054
Wait a minute.

30:32.681 --> 30:35.517
You're all acting suspiciously.

30:35.601 --> 30:37.561
Are you into stocks?
I have some good info.

30:37.645 --> 30:39.355
- For your ears only.
- For real?

30:40.147 --> 30:43.859
I'm hurt. You're hiding something
from us, aren't you?

30:43.943 --> 30:44.944
How dare you!

31:00.668 --> 31:02.211
- Is he okay?
- Sorry.

31:02.586 --> 31:04.505
I'm sorry, Min-su.

31:04.588 --> 31:05.965
Why did he slap him?

31:07.591 --> 31:10.261
Why did you slap him,
White Blood Cell?

31:13.180 --> 31:14.682
- Hello.
- You're here.

31:15.391 --> 31:16.517
Come and sit down.

31:18.519 --> 31:19.770
Hurry and take a seat.

31:46.672 --> 31:49.800
We get the chills
when you act like that at work.

31:50.634 --> 31:52.928
We all tiptoe around you.

31:53.679 --> 31:56.015
In-house couples get caught

31:56.098 --> 31:58.392
because they can't hide
how they feel.

31:58.600 --> 32:01.854
Even if we go to such lengths
to cover up for you

32:01.937 --> 32:03.856
you're making things so obvious.

32:04.523 --> 32:07.693
Why don't you two
fill each other's glasses?

32:21.707 --> 32:23.500
Now repeat after me.

32:24.084 --> 32:25.502
"I am sorry."

32:26.378 --> 32:28.589
It may feel weird and embarrassing

32:28.672 --> 32:31.633
but this is what
I make my kids do after they fight.

32:31.717 --> 32:34.303
Give it a go. "I am sorry."

32:36.638 --> 32:37.931
- I'm sorry.
- I'm sorry.

32:38.807 --> 32:39.933
"I love you."

32:43.145 --> 32:44.605
- I love you.
- I love you.

32:44.980 --> 32:46.648
Now clink glasses.

32:53.364 --> 32:55.282
- Well done.
- Bravo.

32:55.366 --> 32:57.493
- It's all done.
- Congratulations.

32:58.160 --> 33:01.580
I guess it was
a serious fight this time.

33:02.664 --> 33:03.707
What was it about?

33:16.929 --> 33:19.723
Of course, you must marry
if you want to be happy.

33:19.807 --> 33:23.602
You work like crazy all day long
just to return to an empty home.

33:23.977 --> 33:26.063
How is that a happy life? Am I wrong?

33:26.146 --> 33:28.107
That's the best moment of my day.

33:28.190 --> 33:30.401
I suffer all day long
with work and people

33:30.484 --> 33:32.861
but thinking of going home
to even more people

33:33.362 --> 33:34.613
sounds horrible.

33:34.863 --> 33:37.491
Ms. Yoon. Do we give you a hard time?

33:37.574 --> 33:39.159
She's saying

33:39.243 --> 33:42.871
we all find happiness
in different things.

33:43.205 --> 33:46.542
I've been dating my boyfriend
for over ten years

33:46.625 --> 33:48.127
but I don't want to marry him.

33:48.419 --> 33:50.129
He doesn't have a stable income

33:50.212 --> 33:53.006
and he travels to find inspiration
out of the blue.

33:53.090 --> 33:55.300
How could I ask
a free spirit like him

33:55.384 --> 33:57.886
to buy an apartment
and have kids with me?

33:57.970 --> 34:01.974
Yes, but if you're in love,
you want to be together

34:02.057 --> 34:03.642
and plan a future.

34:03.725 --> 34:06.353
Doesn't that make you want to marry?

34:06.437 --> 34:07.855
- That's exactly it.
- Yes.

34:08.230 --> 34:11.191
White Blood Cell,
if that's what you think marriage is

34:11.275 --> 34:12.526
don't ever get married.

34:12.609 --> 34:14.445
Marriage is the real deal.

34:15.070 --> 34:17.865
Did your dream come true
when you got a girlfriend in college?

34:18.532 --> 34:19.700
No, right?

34:19.783 --> 34:21.952
Did finding a job
make you a cool adult?

34:22.035 --> 34:24.872
It didn't.
Life is still gloomy and hard.

34:24.955 --> 34:26.123
Marriage is the same.

34:26.206 --> 34:28.750
Does that mean you shouldn't go
to college or get a job?

34:28.834 --> 34:32.254
You speak so negatively,
but you're happily married.

34:32.504 --> 34:34.715
You can build a life together.

34:35.174 --> 34:37.092
Marriage is different
from college or work.

34:37.176 --> 34:39.094
Those are choices you make yourself.

34:39.178 --> 34:41.263
Marriage is a compromise
between two people.

34:41.346 --> 34:43.140
- It's double the risk.
- Yes.

34:43.974 --> 34:46.268
"Risk"? Do you think
marriage is an audit case

34:46.351 --> 34:48.645
where you calculate every risk?

34:48.729 --> 34:52.691
Of course. My life is at stake,
so I must calculate every risk.

34:52.774 --> 34:55.944
By what standard are you calculating
what the pros and cons are?

34:56.528 --> 34:58.614
Marriage isn't about calculations

34:58.697 --> 35:00.240
but a matter of trust
between two people.

35:00.324 --> 35:03.327
Trust alone isn't enough.
You need conviction.

35:04.661 --> 35:06.955
So you're saying
you have no conviction in me.

35:07.039 --> 35:08.165
Hey, Mr. Noh.

35:08.457 --> 35:09.625
It's not that.

35:09.958 --> 35:14.004
I cannot be certain of the effect
marriage will have on my life!

35:14.087 --> 35:16.757
- Ms. Joo.
- How will you build that conviction?

35:17.007 --> 35:19.384
What can I do
to give you that certainty?

35:34.274 --> 35:35.984
Gosh, that was delicious.

35:36.068 --> 35:37.277
I'm so full.

35:37.361 --> 35:38.862
Hey, pull it together, man.

35:38.946 --> 35:40.906
What's for round two?
It's been a while since we've been...

35:40.989 --> 35:42.908
- Thank you for dinner.
- Thank you!

35:42.991 --> 35:44.868
- Thank you.
- Please excuse us first.

35:44.952 --> 35:46.620
Let's call it a night!

35:46.703 --> 35:48.622
- Goodbye.
- I love going to a karaoke room.

35:48.705 --> 35:49.915
- Go now.
- Right?

35:50.666 --> 35:52.167
- Goodbye.
- Bye!

35:59.258 --> 36:00.676
Should I call a cab?

36:00.759 --> 36:02.928
Yes, we should. It's too far to walk.

36:06.056 --> 36:07.891
So you must feel certain about cabs.

36:23.532 --> 36:25.200
Hello, you've reached Joo In-a.

36:30.080 --> 36:31.164
Yes, and?

37:17.294 --> 37:18.629
Thank you for coming.

37:22.924 --> 37:25.636
- Take your time to eat.
- Mr. Noh, one moment.

37:30.432 --> 37:31.683
- Yes?
- Well...

37:32.267 --> 37:33.602
Is she holding the wake
only for one day?

37:33.685 --> 37:35.062
Is she not accepting
any condolence money?

37:38.398 --> 37:40.692
No, she's keeping it simple.

37:41.526 --> 37:42.944
But still, it's too empty.

37:43.904 --> 37:45.906
She told me not to contact
anyone else at work

37:45.989 --> 37:47.574
so we came by ourselves.

37:48.116 --> 37:49.326
But I feel bad.

37:50.118 --> 37:51.870
I heard they had no real contact.

37:52.913 --> 37:54.331
Ms. Joo seems almost too calm.

37:54.790 --> 37:57.125
That's enough. She must have
a lot on her mind.

37:59.044 --> 38:00.212
It's the Vice President.

38:03.048 --> 38:04.091
Hello.

38:31.535 --> 38:33.286
Did you return to Korea for this?

38:34.454 --> 38:35.914
You didn't have to.

38:36.248 --> 38:37.958
I've been living in Seoul recently.

38:39.084 --> 38:41.586
I'm planning to work
on the medical foundation again.

38:42.379 --> 38:43.714
Good for you.

38:44.673 --> 38:45.757
That's a great decision.

38:48.552 --> 38:52.055
I can see that Mr. Noh
is right here for you to lean on.

38:55.517 --> 38:56.560
I mean it.

38:57.269 --> 38:59.354
I'm glad that you have
someone like Mr. Noh Ki-jun...

39:01.565 --> 39:02.566
in your life.

39:10.282 --> 39:11.283
Bye, now.

39:11.992 --> 39:12.993
Bye.

39:42.606 --> 39:44.900
- Are you all right?
- Yes.

39:45.859 --> 39:48.320
The hospital put these together.

39:48.987 --> 39:49.988
They were your father's.

39:52.407 --> 39:53.825
You must be tired.

39:54.242 --> 39:56.328
You should go home now.
You have work tomorrow.

39:56.411 --> 39:57.746
I can do the funeral procession
on my own.

39:57.829 --> 40:00.373
I'll stay.
I already took the day off tomorrow.

40:00.457 --> 40:04.586
- Just go home. I'm fine.
- Come on. I'm really okay.

40:07.964 --> 40:10.091
Your tea's cold.
Let me get you a new one.

41:11.444 --> 41:13.196
What is this, really?

41:16.491 --> 41:18.159
How ridiculous.

41:23.248 --> 41:24.499
I hate him...

41:27.377 --> 41:28.545
yet I pity him.

41:30.839 --> 41:32.966
I pity him, yet I can't forgive him.

41:34.926 --> 41:37.345
I haven't forgiven him,
but he has already passed away.

41:40.599 --> 41:41.933
Seriously.

41:43.101 --> 41:45.812
What do I do?

41:50.692 --> 41:51.776
I can't believe it.

42:22.057 --> 42:24.893
I can just go home and sleep.

42:24.976 --> 42:27.020
You haven't had
anything to eat all day.

42:27.103 --> 42:29.648
I'll only be relieved
after I see you eat something.

42:30.231 --> 42:31.650
What are you going to make me?

42:32.192 --> 42:33.485
Yes, right?

42:33.568 --> 42:34.819
That's true.

42:34.903 --> 42:36.529
- You have a point.
- Yes.

42:36.780 --> 42:37.822
Go on.

42:38.698 --> 42:39.783
Hey.

42:40.659 --> 42:41.993
Hey! Gosh!

42:42.077 --> 42:43.745
Why did you change the passcode?

42:43.828 --> 42:46.039
I got it wrong five times,
so I had to wait five minutes.

42:46.122 --> 42:47.874
- Hello.
- Hello.

42:48.249 --> 42:49.751
- You two were together!
- Right?

42:49.834 --> 42:51.336
- I'm glad.
- Yes.

42:51.419 --> 42:52.754
- Hello.
- Have you all been well?

42:53.046 --> 42:54.172
- Yes.
- Yes.

42:54.255 --> 42:56.007
Why didn't you call me first?

42:56.091 --> 42:59.010
Why did you punch in numbers
recklessly only to complain?

42:59.386 --> 43:01.304
- Why did you change the number?
- Yes, why? How dare you?

43:01.388 --> 43:03.223
- You should've told us first.
- It's my home.

43:03.306 --> 43:04.557
- What's with you?
- Please excuse me.

43:04.641 --> 43:06.935
- No, stay.
- No, come and eat.

43:07.018 --> 43:09.646
- We brought good food.
- Yes.

43:12.107 --> 43:13.483
So what's all this?

43:20.031 --> 43:21.700
We heard the news.

43:21.950 --> 43:24.369
It must've been so shocking.

43:24.619 --> 43:27.831
We wanted to visit you at the wake,
but the funeral was already done.

43:27.914 --> 43:31.084
Ki-jun made a huge scene
and told us not to show up.

43:31.167 --> 43:33.003
We thought you couldn't have eaten
after that shock.

43:33.086 --> 43:34.379
Here's porridge
to help with digestion.

43:34.629 --> 43:35.797
Have some dongchimi with it.

43:35.880 --> 43:40.010
Have some before it gets cold.
I even chopped the liver to make it.

43:40.593 --> 43:43.013
- Eat up.
- Leave it. We'll have it on our own.

43:43.096 --> 43:45.890
What? She has to eat it
while it's hot to enjoy it.

43:45.974 --> 43:47.809
Yes, thank you.

43:56.443 --> 43:58.611
It's delicious.
It's giving me strength.

43:59.654 --> 44:01.114
- I knew it.
- I told you so.

44:01.197 --> 44:03.658
- I should've added wild chives.
- It's good.

44:03.742 --> 44:05.618
- Eat a lot more.
- She's going to get sick!

44:05.702 --> 44:07.662
- Ki-jun, bring water for her meal.
- Yes, hurry.

44:07.746 --> 44:09.080
Come on. Move it.

44:09.497 --> 44:12.459
- It must've been hectic.
- I bet.

44:12.542 --> 44:14.669
I've done a one-day wake
when my grandfather-in-law passed

44:14.753 --> 44:17.297
and it was tighter and more hectic
compared to three-day ones.

44:17.380 --> 44:19.632
Things are more hectic now
than at the wake, okay?

44:19.716 --> 44:22.177
Did Ki-jun actually help out?

44:22.469 --> 44:25.263
I mean, he grew up only with women

44:25.346 --> 44:27.432
I'm not sure
if he can even perform as a man.

44:27.724 --> 44:30.685
Will you try to pick out
proper words when you speak?

44:31.186 --> 44:33.730
- Okay?
- What about my words?

44:33.813 --> 44:35.190
- Eat up.
- Which words?

44:35.273 --> 44:36.399
- Eat.
- "Perform" was kind of odd.

44:36.483 --> 44:37.734
- Performing as a man?
- Performing?

44:37.817 --> 44:39.736
- Performing as a man!
- Hey.

44:39.819 --> 44:40.904
- Hey, man.
- Stop.

44:40.987 --> 44:42.322
You're a big man now.

44:42.405 --> 44:44.532
- There are other words!
- Yes, sure.

44:44.616 --> 44:47.077
Goodness, you're such a man!

44:47.160 --> 44:48.369
A man who can perform.

44:48.828 --> 44:52.165
- Yes, "perform."
- Oh, boy. How adorable.

44:52.248 --> 44:54.626
Hey, that should be enough.
You should go.

44:54.709 --> 44:55.960
Give this to her.

45:06.179 --> 45:07.180
Cab fare.

45:09.140 --> 45:11.267
I can't reimburse anything
before 10 p.m.

45:11.351 --> 45:14.395
There's not much difference.
Just do it.

45:33.248 --> 45:34.666
Let me return the paperwork.

45:35.667 --> 45:37.919
Why hasn't this gone through?

45:38.002 --> 45:39.963
The name on the seal certification
is the previous CEO's.

45:40.046 --> 45:41.714
I'll need one
under the current CEO's name.

45:42.507 --> 45:45.468
Does that mean
I'll need more paperwork?

45:45.552 --> 45:46.719
It's written over there.

45:49.055 --> 45:51.850
Customer number nine,
please come to window four.

46:05.905 --> 46:08.324
If you want a new certification
of the seal impression

46:08.408 --> 46:10.577
you have to go
to a register office, not here.

46:11.369 --> 46:15.123
There, apply for the continued use
of the seal registration card.

46:15.415 --> 46:16.708
Do you have the corporate seal?

46:17.167 --> 46:19.586
You need to take that
to apply for it right away.

46:20.170 --> 46:21.171
Thank you.

46:22.172 --> 46:23.214
Goodbye, then.

46:36.769 --> 46:37.770
Ms. Park.

46:51.034 --> 46:52.160
Where do you work right now?

46:53.578 --> 46:56.247
Why do you ask?

47:06.049 --> 47:07.258
Call me if you'd like to join me.

47:07.342 --> 47:08.801
JEI MEDICAL FOUNDATION
JEON JAE-YEOL

47:11.179 --> 47:12.639
This is a recruitment offer.

47:15.934 --> 47:16.935
Do I...

47:18.728 --> 47:20.605
Do I really deserve this?

47:24.567 --> 47:26.069
I need a talented employee.

47:27.153 --> 47:28.238
That's all.

47:34.285 --> 47:36.955
So this is what I want to emphasize.

47:37.455 --> 47:39.082
When you first joined the company

47:39.165 --> 47:42.585
you were lucky enough
to have me as your direct superior.

47:42.669 --> 47:45.505
Hence, you got the chance
to learn so much from me.

47:45.588 --> 47:48.049
Also, whenever you had
a tough and arduous time...

47:48.132 --> 47:49.592
Cut to the chase, Se-young.

47:49.842 --> 47:51.010
What's your point?

47:51.094 --> 47:53.763
The Audit Team is going to be
separated from the division, right?

47:54.138 --> 47:58.017
So in an effort to give more power
to the Audit Team

47:58.351 --> 48:00.144
we've decided to promote the head.

48:00.937 --> 48:03.398
And you already qualify
more than enough.

48:06.567 --> 48:09.696
I'm saying, you're going to be
a senior managing director.

48:16.536 --> 48:17.537
Thank you.

48:18.788 --> 48:19.914
- Thank you.
- Congratulations!

48:19.998 --> 48:21.165
Congratulations, Ms. Joo.

48:23.960 --> 48:26.546
Now, Senior Managing Director Joo.
Please share a word with us.

48:28.172 --> 48:31.050
I owe it all to you.

48:31.426 --> 48:32.844
I share my deepest gratitude.

48:33.094 --> 48:36.097
Goodness, don't be so humble.

48:36.180 --> 48:39.183
Boo! Be more honest!
That was so boring!

48:39.267 --> 48:41.352
That was so boring.

48:43.604 --> 48:44.605
"Boring"?

48:50.528 --> 48:51.946
Are you looking

48:53.031 --> 48:54.949
to have fun in the office right now?

48:59.662 --> 49:00.705
In that case

49:01.664 --> 49:02.874
how about this?

49:04.459 --> 49:05.460
Like this.

49:08.254 --> 49:09.297
What do you think?

49:14.594 --> 49:15.595
How's that?

49:18.723 --> 49:19.807
Keep it up!

49:19.891 --> 49:21.934
- All right!
- You're the best!

49:26.731 --> 49:29.484
Senior Managing Director Joo,
you don't have to do this.

49:30.276 --> 49:32.195
I don't think
I'll be able to check on it often.

49:32.278 --> 49:33.821
I'm getting my own office.

49:34.489 --> 49:36.908
Wow, your very own office.

49:37.367 --> 49:40.244
- That's awesome.
- Hey, are you free tonight?

49:40.661 --> 49:41.788
My treat.

49:42.330 --> 49:44.374
Or do you want to come to my place?

49:44.457 --> 49:46.501
I think I can recreate
the pasta we had last time

49:46.584 --> 49:48.086
so I bought a lot of ingredients.

49:48.169 --> 49:51.172
Gosh, the senior managing director
even knows how to cook?

49:54.217 --> 49:55.468
But what a shame.

49:55.551 --> 49:56.677
I have to go to my mom's place.

49:56.761 --> 49:59.263
They're making a big batch of kimchi,
so I have to go and help.

49:59.347 --> 50:00.390
Is that so?

50:00.807 --> 50:03.518
I can't help it, then.
Go and help them out, okay?

50:04.435 --> 50:05.728
- What?
- Where are you going?

50:05.812 --> 50:06.854
To the office.

50:08.439 --> 50:11.275
- We're at work. Hands off.
- No one is around. No one's here.

50:12.235 --> 50:14.404
- You aren't mad, are you?
- I am.

50:15.196 --> 50:18.366
Ki-jun, you'll find
more napa cabbage outside.

50:18.449 --> 50:19.450
Bring them in.

50:20.410 --> 50:21.702
- Hurry up.
- Wait.

50:22.453 --> 50:23.830
Are you trying to give away
free kimchi?

50:24.372 --> 50:25.915
Why are you making so much kimchi?

50:26.165 --> 50:27.917
The kids don't eat
a lot of kimchi anyway.

50:28.167 --> 50:30.044
We have
another family member this year.

50:30.128 --> 50:32.547
What? Another family member? Who?

50:33.089 --> 50:35.216
Mom, it hasn't happened yet.

50:35.299 --> 50:38.511
What? What are you talking about?
Why is our family getting bigger?

50:38.594 --> 50:40.888
We're talking about your Ms. Joo.

50:42.014 --> 50:43.433
It's her.

50:43.516 --> 50:45.309
She's practically family now.

50:45.601 --> 50:47.645
- Goodness.
- While we're at it

50:47.728 --> 50:49.689
do you have any specific plans?

50:49.772 --> 50:51.691
It's not easy to secure a good date
for a nice venue.

50:51.774 --> 50:54.360
Why is everyone jumping so far ahead?

50:54.444 --> 50:55.486
Also...

50:55.903 --> 50:57.864
she'll be really busy for a while.

50:58.698 --> 50:59.699
- Why?
- Why?

51:05.246 --> 51:07.373
She got promoted
to senior managing director.

51:07.957 --> 51:10.418
Do you know how busy they are
at a major company like ours?

51:10.668 --> 51:12.336
That's who In-a is.

51:12.420 --> 51:14.172
She's a woman of great caliber.

51:14.255 --> 51:16.799
How dare you try to lock up
a great person like her

51:16.883 --> 51:19.302
as the daughter-in-law
of a nameless family like ours? Gosh.

51:19.385 --> 51:22.513
Good grief.
What a great boyfriend you are.

51:23.055 --> 51:24.932
But that's really amazing.

51:25.224 --> 51:28.060
Wait, a senior managing director
is right below the vice president.

51:28.144 --> 51:29.687
That's not a job for just anyone.

51:29.770 --> 51:32.231
Of course not.
My In-a isn't just anyone.

51:32.732 --> 51:34.358
I guess she'll be busy.

51:34.942 --> 51:37.278
The least I can do
is not stand in her way

51:37.487 --> 51:39.822
if I can't be of help to her
who is about to do great work.

51:39.906 --> 51:43.075
They'll figure it out on their own
in good time.

51:43.159 --> 51:46.704
We'll figure it out on our own
so don't worry too much, okay?

52:21.989 --> 52:23.074
It's good.

52:58.568 --> 52:59.610
In-a!

53:01.237 --> 53:02.989
Hey, what's going on? What is it?

53:03.322 --> 53:04.991
- Is something going on?
- What's this apron?

53:06.617 --> 53:07.618
Oh, this.

53:08.286 --> 53:10.663
I had to run out
in the middle of making kimchi.

53:11.205 --> 53:15.001
I mean, you've never called me out
so suddenly like this.

53:15.084 --> 53:16.544
I have something to say, Ki-jun.

53:18.713 --> 53:19.714
What is it?

53:25.761 --> 53:26.762
Well...

53:28.222 --> 53:29.849
It'll be like it always was

53:30.641 --> 53:31.934
but I'll be even busier from now on.

53:32.935 --> 53:34.937
I'll have to get to work early,
work overtime often

53:35.021 --> 53:36.397
and have to work
outside the office, too.

53:37.398 --> 53:40.192
I won't be able to text
or call back as I do now.

53:41.444 --> 53:42.778
And above all...

53:44.655 --> 53:45.865
I think...

53:47.325 --> 53:48.367
my personality may become

53:49.535 --> 53:51.329
even worse than what it is now.

53:52.330 --> 53:54.665
My new position comes with that much
responsibility and pressure.

53:55.708 --> 54:01.005
I might become much pickier,
more impatient and easily angered

54:01.088 --> 54:02.632
and even try
to vent my stress on you.

54:06.886 --> 54:07.928
And?

54:10.264 --> 54:11.641
What are you trying to say?

54:18.773 --> 54:20.024
Do you want to live with me?

54:22.777 --> 54:24.528
Let's try living together.

54:27.698 --> 54:29.867
- Are you asking me to move in?
- Yes.

54:36.207 --> 54:37.958
Why did you suddenly get this idea?

54:39.627 --> 54:40.711
Today

54:42.004 --> 54:43.589
I was thrilled to hear the news.

54:44.590 --> 54:47.093
Then you were the first person
I wanted to share it with.

54:48.010 --> 54:50.554
I celebrated alone at home,
but it wasn't that fun.

54:50.971 --> 54:53.349
And the pasta wasn't as good
as the time we had it together.

54:54.433 --> 54:55.685
At some point

54:56.185 --> 54:59.230
I must've gotten used to sharing
my joy and sadness with you.

55:01.941 --> 55:03.234
But I never realized it.

55:04.235 --> 55:07.488
I was already imagining
my everyday life with you

55:07.780 --> 55:08.781
but I...

55:09.281 --> 55:14.036
I just got tied up by the idea
that I shouldn't get married.

55:16.956 --> 55:17.998
Honestly

55:19.250 --> 55:22.086
I'm not sure
if I can deal with marriage.

55:23.504 --> 55:25.965
My father
could not keep his family together

55:26.048 --> 55:28.509
and my mom never became a part
of the thing called marriage.

55:29.260 --> 55:30.344
It's a concept

55:31.679 --> 55:33.764
that never existed in my life

55:35.015 --> 55:36.308
so it's true that I feel uncertain.

55:38.102 --> 55:39.145
But despite that

55:40.479 --> 55:42.314
I want to be with you, Ki-jun.

55:43.774 --> 55:45.693
So I want to take my time

55:46.902 --> 55:50.322
and start by living together.

56:06.756 --> 56:09.008
What's going on?
You have to tell me yes or no.

56:09.091 --> 56:11.469
I'm rambling on all by myself,
and I'm starting to feel embarrassed.

56:15.723 --> 56:16.724
How much worse...

56:18.642 --> 56:20.186
will your personality become?

56:23.105 --> 56:24.231
A little bit.

56:29.737 --> 56:31.822
Okay, let's stay together

56:32.531 --> 56:33.532
no matter what that life is.

56:57.807 --> 56:58.849
Wait.

56:59.433 --> 57:01.018
- Why?
- Gosh, you smell.

57:31.757 --> 57:35.219
Just like that,
our secret private life began.

57:40.432 --> 57:43.310
It was filled with ordinary
yet precious everyday moments.

57:47.731 --> 57:49.483
Gold bars!

57:49.900 --> 57:50.985
Hey.

57:51.527 --> 57:52.903
Merry Christmas.

57:54.655 --> 57:57.157
And there were moments
that shimmered like a dream.

58:12.131 --> 58:14.091
But there were dark sides
that were better off not known...

58:14.633 --> 58:15.801
Gosh, it's so hot.

58:22.349 --> 58:23.434
Why is it so cold?

58:26.312 --> 58:27.479
So cold.

58:28.564 --> 58:29.648
Gosh, it's chilly.

58:29.857 --> 58:30.983
So hot.

58:32.902 --> 58:33.903
Wait, what?

58:35.279 --> 58:37.031
Hey, the temperature.

58:37.448 --> 58:39.325
Oh, come on. Why does it keep...

58:39.408 --> 58:41.619
Why is this house so cold?

58:43.078 --> 58:45.247
See? This is why it's so cold.

58:45.497 --> 58:47.333
...and unexpected
temperature differences.

58:48.208 --> 58:49.376
Wait, hey.

58:52.504 --> 58:55.716
I told you to leave the bathroom door
wide open over and over again.

58:55.799 --> 58:57.968
- It gets damp.
- It's winter, not summer.

58:58.052 --> 59:00.804
And I hate smelling the drain
in the living room when it's open!

59:00.888 --> 59:02.681
Are you going to clean it up
when it develops mold?

59:02.765 --> 59:04.350
Yes! When did I not do it?

59:05.601 --> 59:06.977
The most critical thing was this.

59:11.732 --> 59:13.609
The biggest difficulty between us

59:14.068 --> 59:15.319
was that we also shared
our work life.

59:15.402 --> 59:17.071
SENIOR MANAGING DIRECTOR JOO IN-A

59:17.196 --> 59:18.572
For the official schedule tomorrow

59:18.656 --> 59:20.950
you can just attend the event
before the actual ceremony.

59:22.576 --> 59:25.996
You seem upset.
Is there a problem with the schedule?

59:26.080 --> 59:27.831
No, it's not that.

59:29.708 --> 59:31.085
I shouldn't be like this.

59:32.127 --> 59:35.297
Ms. Ahn, are you aware
of the hungry judge effect?

59:35.839 --> 59:37.549
- Sorry?
- It's a study that says

59:37.633 --> 59:40.094
judges tend to give strict rulings
before their breaks

59:40.177 --> 59:44.098
and more tolerant ones
after they come back from lunch.

59:44.807 --> 59:48.727
It means
something seemingly petty like hunger

59:49.561 --> 59:51.772
can affect your work.

59:53.357 --> 59:54.858
Ms. Joo, are you hungry?

59:55.275 --> 59:56.402
No, it's not that.

59:56.819 --> 59:59.863
It's just that hard to differentiate
between work and private life.

01:00:00.155 --> 01:00:02.116
If you are,
I can prepare something...

01:00:02.199 --> 01:00:03.951
Oh, not at all.

01:00:04.243 --> 01:00:06.078
- Please continue.
- Yes.

01:00:06.537 --> 01:00:08.080
- So before the ceremony...
- That's true.

01:00:08.205 --> 01:00:11.500
Drawing the line
between work and personal life

01:00:11.583 --> 01:00:13.544
is never as simple as it sounds.

01:00:13.627 --> 01:00:14.878
Da-young, one iced Americano, please.

01:00:14.962 --> 01:00:16.630
Add another shot
and fill it up with ice.

01:00:17.673 --> 01:00:19.258
Yes, okay.

01:00:19.341 --> 01:00:20.968
Oh, come on.

01:00:22.886 --> 01:00:24.722
- Here it is.
- Yes, thank you.

01:00:25.889 --> 01:00:27.474
- Hey.
- My gosh.

01:00:28.017 --> 01:00:29.435
Did you get into a fight with her?

01:00:32.813 --> 01:00:34.106
You know what?

01:00:35.065 --> 01:00:37.317
I still can't get used
to you working here.

01:00:40.320 --> 01:00:41.697
Is it that obvious?

01:00:41.780 --> 01:00:43.073
Totally obvious.

01:00:43.157 --> 01:00:45.284
Smile a little.
You're practically broadcasting it.

01:00:47.119 --> 01:00:48.120
Okay.

01:00:50.998 --> 01:00:51.999
Hey, there.

01:01:11.310 --> 01:01:12.853
Gosh. Seriously.

01:01:22.905 --> 01:01:24.281
I was a little too harsh...

01:01:28.368 --> 01:01:30.621
I'm sorry.
It wasn't even a big deal...

01:01:32.247 --> 01:01:33.874
No, why should I apologize first?

01:01:34.666 --> 01:01:36.543
Yes, I was wrong.

01:01:37.002 --> 01:01:38.087
I don't want to do it.

01:01:39.588 --> 01:01:40.631
Jeez.

01:01:41.381 --> 01:01:42.424
Did they get into a fight?

01:01:42.966 --> 01:01:44.218
Should I just say it first?

01:01:44.968 --> 01:01:46.595
Yes, I'll say it first.

01:01:46.678 --> 01:01:50.766
We clash with personal emotions
countless times a day at work.

01:01:51.809 --> 01:01:52.893
Darn it.

01:02:04.154 --> 01:02:06.115
And those feelings affect our work.

01:02:09.701 --> 01:02:10.828
JEI MEDICAL FOUNDATION
JEON JAE-YEOL

01:02:10.911 --> 01:02:12.037
And because of work

01:02:12.663 --> 01:02:14.456
your feelings falter once again.

01:02:25.217 --> 01:02:28.428
Perhaps separating
work and private life

01:02:28.971 --> 01:02:30.639
isn't about drawing a hard line

01:02:31.265 --> 01:02:34.643
but constantly trying
to keep the balance.

01:02:40.899 --> 01:02:42.109
Manager Noh.

01:02:42.192 --> 01:02:45.028
The first diagram in the report
needs to be revised.

01:02:47.406 --> 01:02:48.699
Yes, Ms. Joo.

01:02:49.616 --> 01:02:50.784
Excuse me.

01:02:50.868 --> 01:02:51.869
He used it!

01:02:52.161 --> 01:02:53.287
Director Hwang

01:02:53.370 --> 01:02:55.497
used his corporate card again
at a hotel on a business trip!

01:02:55.581 --> 01:02:57.583
Get there now.
You need to catch him red-handed.

01:02:57.666 --> 01:02:58.750
Oh, no.

01:02:58.834 --> 01:03:00.878
Everyone except for Mr. Noh
has work out of the office

01:03:00.961 --> 01:03:02.171
so we have no other people.

01:03:22.191 --> 01:03:23.192
Leaving so soon?

01:03:29.114 --> 01:03:30.699
The ice has melted just enough

01:03:30.949 --> 01:03:32.659
so the aroma should be
at its best now.

01:03:33.660 --> 01:03:34.703
Feels like a shame to leave it.

01:03:38.457 --> 01:03:39.625
You can have it.

01:03:50.886 --> 01:03:51.970
She just left.

01:04:03.232 --> 01:04:04.524
His side has entered, too.

01:05:22.060 --> 01:05:24.604
Hello, we're from the Audit Team.

01:05:25.188 --> 01:05:26.273
Director Hwang.

01:05:26.356 --> 01:05:28.400
I don't think
your corporate card covers

01:05:29.234 --> 01:05:31.111
your date expenses.

01:05:36.158 --> 01:05:38.410
It's always much more fun
to do the field work.

01:05:38.577 --> 01:05:40.454
We had great teamwork today, Ms. Joo.

01:05:40.537 --> 01:05:41.705
Yes.

01:05:42.247 --> 01:05:44.374
We're done with work, so give it now.

01:05:48.503 --> 01:05:50.172
I'm hungry. Do you want to go eat?

01:05:50.422 --> 01:05:52.215
It's chilly,
so how about pork backbone stew?

01:05:52.299 --> 01:05:53.675
We'll have it sizzling hot.

01:05:53.759 --> 01:05:56.094
We're here at a hotel, so let's go
to a fine dining restaurant.

01:06:03.018 --> 01:06:04.561
That's not funny. What is that?

01:06:04.644 --> 01:06:06.813
Don't even. You just smiled.

01:06:06.897 --> 01:06:08.190
You did. Look.

01:06:08.273 --> 01:06:10.359
- You smiled.
- Yes, because my boss told a joke.

01:06:10.442 --> 01:06:12.527
Whatever. I know you found it funny.

01:06:13.445 --> 01:06:15.906
- Let's eat the backbone stew.
- That sounds great.

01:06:15.989 --> 01:06:19.534
- And I'm sorry.
- For what?

01:06:19.910 --> 01:06:20.994
This morning.

01:06:23.080 --> 01:06:25.540
Yes, I felt bad, too.
I lashed out at you.

01:06:26.458 --> 01:06:30.295
- Let's not fight, okay?
- Yes, let's not fight anymore.

01:06:37.219 --> 01:06:38.512
Let's go.

01:06:41.973 --> 01:06:43.100
I love stew.

01:06:55.487 --> 01:06:58.365
FILING FOR LOVE

01:06:58.448 --> 01:06:59.658
Here we go.

01:06:59.908 --> 01:07:02.661
GUEST APPEARANCE BY JANG HYUK-JIN

01:07:03.578 --> 01:07:05.122
Can you follow that car?

01:07:05.205 --> 01:07:06.623
One second.

01:07:07.332 --> 01:07:08.834
Don't get so close to James...

01:07:14.297 --> 01:07:16.383
You can't look disheveled
in front of your head.

01:07:18.260 --> 01:07:21.847
You can't look disheveled in front...
Sorry.

01:07:23.849 --> 01:07:24.891
Cut!

01:07:25.392 --> 01:07:26.435
Wait.

01:07:27.686 --> 01:07:29.062
He snapped it.

01:07:29.855 --> 01:07:30.939
I caught it.

01:07:33.275 --> 01:07:35.444
WAIT, I WASN'T SUPPOSED TO GET IT

01:07:38.321 --> 01:07:39.531
Mission success!

01:07:42.534 --> 01:07:44.536
Why is this so easy to win?

01:07:45.871 --> 01:07:46.955
My gosh.

01:07:57.007 --> 01:07:58.091
Don't overreact.

01:07:58.550 --> 01:08:00.760
Don't worry about Mr. Ahn.

01:08:00.969 --> 01:08:02.262
I'm sorry, I'll go again.

01:08:05.724 --> 01:08:08.226
Salt? No, we need to do it over.

01:08:11.271 --> 01:08:13.356
Do something!
You can't just leave him here...

01:08:13.732 --> 01:08:15.692
I'm sorry. One more time.

01:08:15.775 --> 01:08:17.277
I'll do it better!

01:08:17.360 --> 01:08:19.362
Signing of the sale agreement...
What am I saying?

01:08:21.031 --> 01:08:22.616
"Signing of the sale agreement."

01:08:23.241 --> 01:08:25.869
Tomorrow, major subsidiaries
will be signed and sold off.

01:08:26.828 --> 01:08:28.079
The signing of the sale agreement...

01:08:32.792 --> 01:08:35.212
It's like, "We're here already,
so why don't we just kiss?"

01:08:35.295 --> 01:08:36.922
"Should we go there?"

01:08:37.631 --> 01:08:39.257
Wait, why are you laughing?

01:08:39.341 --> 01:08:41.760
- What? It's funny!
- Why did you laugh?

01:08:41.843 --> 01:08:43.094
He just wanted a meal with you.

01:08:46.014 --> 01:08:47.182
Why is this so hot?

01:08:47.265 --> 01:08:48.975
- Yes, it's really hot.
- It's so hot!

01:09:38.984 --> 01:09:40.986
Subtitles by Eunsook Youn
and Jennifer Lim
